  "content": {
    "id": "p49-task3-question",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Consider the quadratic equation with integer coefficients $ax^2+bx+c=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p49-task3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why if $\\Delta=0$, then the roots are rational numbers.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The repeated root is $x=-\\frac{b}{2a}$, a ratio of integers with a nonzero denominator, so it is rational.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{0}}{2a}\\\\x&=-\\frac{b}{2a}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ and $a\\ne0$, this is a ratio of integers with a nonzero denominator. The repeated root is therefore rational.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p49-task3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What can we say about the roots if $\\Delta$ is a perfect square?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Rational roots; distinct if $\\Delta>0$ and repeated if $\\Delta=0$.",
          "worked": "Write $\\Delta=m^2$, where $m$ is a nonnegative integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{m^2}}{2a}\\\\x&=\\frac{-b\\pm m}{2a}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth numerators and the nonzero denominator are integers, so both roots are rational. They are distinct when $m>0$ and coincide when $m=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p49-task3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What can we say about the roots if $\\Delta>0$, but is not a perfect square?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Two distinct irrational real roots.",
          "worked": "The positive nonsquare integer $\\Delta$ has an irrational square root.\n\n$$x=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{\\Delta}}{2a}$$\n\nSince $a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ and $a\\ne0$, both roots are irrational. Since $\\Delta>0$, the roots are real and distinct.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
